                    insight_champion:       `Local champion holds: you defended national share on the non-transferable warung advantage, kept the 13% margin a price war would have erased, and built a moat that compounds. You out-thought a far larger rival instead of out-spending it.`,
                    insight_short:          `You fell short of a defended position. Continental took meaningful share. Re-examine where you fought on its turf — most likely the price war, a thin defend-everywhere line, or under-funding the warung moat.`,
                    insight_pricewar:       `The price war did its damage: matching a USD 70B rival on price collapsed EBITDA toward 6% — you fought on the one battlefield where scale wins. Competing on local value, trust and access beats competing on headline price.`,
                    insight_armed:          `By taking the open partnership you put Continental's brands into all 480.000 warungs on your relationships. The near-term margin came at the cost of your one durable, non-transferable moat — the very asset that made you uncopyable.`,
                    insight_moatlost:       `Moat strength fell dangerously low. The warung network and local fit are the advantage the giant cannot replicate — once eroded by neglect, a poached salesforce or an open partnership, the local champion has little left to defend.`,
                    insight_sharelost:      `You shed roughly the 8–12 points analysts feared. Each point is ≈ Rp95 miliar of revenue — a defensible #1 drifting toward a declining also-ran. The defensive posture had to concentrate force, not spread it.`,
                    insight_compound:       `This is a franchise built to last: share, moat and margin all healthy, the advantage institutionalised and ready to extend into adjacent categories and ASEAN. The next giant's entry can now be met from strength.`,

                    hint_armed:             `You've armed the rival inside your moat — its brands now ride your warung relationships. Going forward, lean hard on institutionalising and deepening local advantage the giant still can't replicate.`,
                    hint_pricewar:          `You're in a price war you can't fund against a USD 70B rival. Stop matching on price; compete on local value, trust and warung access to rebuild margin.`,
                    hint_moat:              `Moat strength is critically low. Fund the warung network and retain the regional managers the giant is raiding — the local advantage lives in those relationships and people.`,
